# Server-authority protocol

The server-authoritative rework replaces the wire. Do not extend, match, or debug pre-rework networking unless the user asks for that code.

Skip it:

- Packet builders, decoders, and `PacketPart` layouts from before this rework
- In-game handlers that parse those frames (`PingHandler`, attack, item, vendor, move)
- MBC region formats as the thing to reproduce on the wire

New sessions live under `Server/Simulation/` on the server and `core/gameplay` plus `core/network` (`GameChannels`, `DtlsSession`) on the client. Presentation scripts may call into those. They do not own the protocol.
